  ("The lobster roll", "Cold with a little mayo, or warm with drawn butter. Locals argue about this one too.", "dish_lobster"),
  ("Boston cream pie", "Invented at the Parker House Hotel in the 1850s and now the official state dessert.", "dish_bcp"),
  ("Parker House rolls", "Soft, buttery folded rolls from the same famous hotel kitchen.", "dish_rolls"),
  ("Oysters", "From Duxbury, Wellfleet and the Cape. Union Oyster House has served them since 1826, making it America's oldest continuously operating restaurant.", "dish_oysters"),
  ("Steamers", "Soft-shell clams steamed in their shells. Pull one out, swish it in the broth, dip it in melted butter. A New England summer ritual.", "dish_steamers"),
